            <ArticleTitle>Efficacy of therapeutic interventions for silent myocardial ischemia and clinical trial benefit.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>479-86</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article reviews the efficacy of medical and revascularization therapeutic interventions directed at the reduction or elimination of silent myocardial The review focuses on the use of standard anti-ischemic medications, including nitrates, calcium antagonists, and beta-blockers. In addition, data suggesting therapeutic benefit of antiplatelet agents are discussed. Finally, the results of studies evaluating the efficacy of revascularization with PTCA and coronary artery bypass graft surgery are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
